  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 56425ae234e5e1f43b907b48f58638db, type: 3}
  rarity: 0
  itemType: 3
  description: "<b>AN ATOMIC CHRISTMAS: THE FIRST EMPTY HOLIDAY TABLES</b>\nFor millions
    of Americans, this December brings a surreal holiday reality: the first Christmas
    without a feast. Following the rapid nationwide rollout of the controversial
    \"Atomic Vaccine,\" which permanently eliminated human hunger, families are staring
    down an unprecedented tradition\u2014the entirely empty dining table.\n\nGone
    are the familiar sights of roasted turkeys, glazed hams, and overflowing cornucopias.
    With the radioactive serum fundamentally altering human metabolism and providing
    endless cellular energy, physical eating has become an obsolete chore rather
    than a festive joy.\n\n\"It feels like a ghost town in my kitchen,\" lamented
    Mary Miller, a suburban housewife. \"We saved hours of cooking, but we lost the
    heart of the holiday. What do we gather around now?\"\n\nWhile the administration
    champions the end of winter food shortages, sociologists warn of a growing cultural
    void. America must now invent new ways to celebrate."
